\section{Conclusion}
We present \tool{}, a tool that leverages LLMs and embeddings to create an interactive interface of automatically-generated histograms for data practitioners to analyze unstructured datasets. Through an observational study with 10 data workers, we validate that the tool can address targeted user needs such as summarizing datasets, identifying outliers and interesting slices of data, and testing hypotheses rapidly and interactively. Participants quickly identified the correct dataset topic, noticed a potentially-concerning asymmetrical data distribution, and found safety violations within the dataset. Finally, we summarize potential use cases and limitations of \tool{} described by these participants. Together, these findings suggest that advancements in LLMs can enable the development of sensemaking tools to better serve data workers.
